  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts. It builds the scene, but I couldn't run it, so the physics, launch and reset behavior is untested. The typecheck passes.\n\n- **Pyramid:** 15 dynamic boxes in rows of 5, 4, 3, 2 and 1, on a static floor box. The physics is the engine's Rapier-based `app.physics`, stepped once per frame with the time step capped at 1/30 s.\n- **Launch:** a heavy ball (mass 12) starts at x=-7. 1.5 s after load, `setVelocity([19, 1.2, 0])` sends it toward the pyramid. The boxes should tumble and settle under physics.\n- **Reset:** pressing Space calls `app.setScene(buildScene())`, which rebuilds every body at its start pose and restarts the 1.5 s timer. I rebuilt the scene because the public body handle has no `setRotation`, so tumbled boxes couldn't be un-rotated any other way. The docs advise against `setScene` for restarts, and I haven't confirmed it clears the old bodies properly.\n- **Look and camera:** the `outdoor-day` look supplies the lighting and shadows. The camera sits at (-1.5, 4.2, 12.5), aimed at the pyramid. I worked out by hand that it should cover both the pyramid and the ball's run from x=-7.\n- **Ready flag:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set on the first `requestAnimationFrame` after `app.ready()`.\n\n",
